%N A322651 Numbers that are sums of one or more consecutive hexagonal pyramidal numbers (A002412).
%C A322651 The first term that occurs in more than one way is a(617) = 185185 = Sum_{k=21 .. 33} A002412(k) = A002412(65). - _Robert Israel_, Aug 05 2026
%H A322651 Robert Israel, <a href="/A322651/b322651.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A322651 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HexagonalPyramidalNumber.html">Hexagonal Pyramidal Number</a>
%p A322651 hps:= [seq(k^2*(k + 2)*(k + 1)/6,k=0..50)]:
%p A322651 M:= hps[-1]-hps[-2]:
%p A322651 S:= select(`<=`,{0,seq(seq(hps[i]-hps[j],j=1..i-1),i=1..50)},M):
%p A322651 sort(convert(S,list)); # _Robert Israel_, Aug 05 2026
